    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109-a1-a3-a1">

                <pb facs="0218" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg148"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 14.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Downing Street,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1799-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 21, 1799.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I send you enclosed the copy of a letter
                    which I have received from the lords commissioners of the admiralty, together
                    with the papers to which it refers; and I have to signify to you his Majesty’s
                    pleasure that if the vessel mentioned in them, (<hi rendition="#italic">the brig
                        Experience,)</hi> should be brought into any port of the United States, you
                    make a formal demand that she be immediately delivered up to you, together with
                    the deserters and seamen who rescued her out of the possession of the prize
                    master, in order that they may be sent to Jamaica, or to some other of his
                    Majesty’s colonies, to be there dealt with agreeably to the law of nations.</p>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Liston.</hi></p>
            </div>
        </body>
